      "writtenOn": "2026-06-16T08:28:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I noticed we are using GetFloatArrayRegion here with a fixed constant_length. What do you think about adding a quick bounds check before doing the copy?\n\nMy worry is that if a user accidentally passes an array from Kotlin that is smaller than {{ member.constant_length }}, JNI will throw an ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException on the JVM, but C++ will continue executing. That would result in us passing an uninitialized array buffer directly into Dawn.\n\nWould it be safer to check env-\u003eGetArrayLength(in) and early-return if it doesn\u0027t match?",
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "494dc8eb_3c8fdf2e",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "generator/templates/art/kotlin_record_conversion.cpp",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 245,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 248,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "                            jsize arrayLength \u003d env-\u003eGetArrayLength(in);\n                            if (arrayLength \u003d\u003d {{ member.constant_length }}) {\n                                auto array \u003d c-\u003eAllocArray\u003cfloat\u003e({{ member.constant_length }});\n                                env-\u003eGetFloatArrayRegion(static_cast\u003cjfloatArray\u003e(in), 0, {{ member.constant_length }}, array);\n                                out \u003d array;\n                            } else {\n                                // If the array length doesn\u0027t match the expected constant length,\n                                // do not proceed to avoid potential crashes or uninitialized data.\n                                // The out variable remains in its default-initialized state (e.g., nullptr).\n                                return;\n                            }\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "944486d8d5fbf142d24da184456ca21b746b9112",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
